 A working Three.js warehouse sandbox built from **Order Picking Dataset from a Warehouse of a Footwear Manufacturing Company**, Mendeley Data v1, Rodrigo Furlan de Assis, DOI [10.17632/pf2w725pw3.1](https://doi.org/10.17632/pf2w725pw3.1), **CC BY 4.0**.
 
 The application includes all 2,292 storage coordinates, 208 product references, four published allocation files, 39,858 normalized wave/order groups from 122,370 customer rows, and a deterministic 10-AMR picking simulation. The default demand window is the first 120 complete source orders. All 21 publisher files were downloaded and SHA-256 verified; no fabricated fallback dataset is used.
+
+## Internal governance and evidence (2026-10-17)
+
+The MVP remains frozen. The [internal review](docs/FINAL_REVIEW.md), [gate register](docs/GATE_REVIEWS.md), and [evaluation contract](docs/EVALUATION_PLAN.md) separate software verification from model/experiment/business validity. All human gate reviews are **PENDING**; no operational validation or policy ranking is approved. The technical evidence does not establish real-world savings or physical accuracy.
+
+Internal QA commands (Python3.10+ standard library for data checks):
+
+```bash
+npm run audit:data
+npm run test:data
+npm test
+npm run validate:scenarios
+npm run evaluate:governance
+npm run build
+npm run test:browser
+npm run check:governance
+```
+
+See the [evidence index](docs/EVIDENCE_INDEX.md) for input hashes, execution logs, limits and review procedure. Existing data interpretation rules and default scenario outcomes were preserved; supported fixes protect source ZIP imports and reject invalid routing endpoints. Stage-gate review and unresolved business/methodological decisions require an identified human.
 
